## Match the data to the resource

| Data | Starting point |
| --- | --- |
| Customer records and relationships | Relational database |
| Files that change during a workload | Persistent volume |
| Uploaded images and exported artifacts | Object storage |
| A recoverable environment state | Snapshot |

## A binding is a connection

The application should receive the right endpoint and credentials through configuration. Keep the binding attached to the application and environment it serves, so a staging release does not accidentally use production data.

## Separate identity from location

A returned URL tells you where to connect. A resource identifier tells you what is being connected. Keep both when recording an operation.

## Check recovery assumptions

Test the recovery path for the data that matters. An application rollback does not necessarily roll back database changes. Read [snapshots](/docs/snapshots) and [deployment recovery](/docs/deployments) as different responsibilities.
